# NorthNarrow — the data directories of root daemons (default, v1)
#
# Lot 283c. A server doing its normal job does not sit in ENGAGED: the
# mass-write arm of the posture's ConfirmedIntrusion leaves out a crossing
# of the kernel's write counters when every file its window counted lies in
# one directory listed here AND the writer's cgroup is one of that
# directory's units (/system.slice/<unit>). A root process outside the unit,
# and the unit writing anywhere else, still count. The counters count every
# write, and the ransomware tracker (NN-L-IMP-001: entropy, renames, copies
# and deletions) judges every crossing, these included.
#
# Service accounts (postgres, mysql, redis, ...) need no entry: their own
# files under /var/lib or their home, in a directory they own, are told by
# ownership. A person's ~/.cache by its owner.
#
# The shipped list is content of the release: the agent applies the copy it
# was built with whenever /etc/northnarrow/daemon-data.v1 is not that copy
# (an edit is an ERROR and a signed `default_list_modified` at every boot);
# install.sh installs it. The operator adds directories in the signed
# overlay /etc/northnarrow/mass-write-carveout.local, one line each:
#
#   +<unit>.service <directory>/
#
# Format, one entry per line; `#` starts a comment:
#
#   <unit>.service <directory>/
#
# A directory may not lie inside another listed one or hold one, nor be too
# broad (`/`, a top-level directory, a user's tree, /var/tmp, /dev/shm,
# /run/user).

containerd.service /var/lib/containerd/
docker.service /var/lib/docker/
kubelet.service /var/lib/kubelet/
etcd.service /var/lib/etcd/

# k3s runs containerd and the kubelet inside its own unit. Lot 283a measured
# its crossings in the kubelet's directory, the CNI results and containerd's
# task state under /run/k3s, beside /var/lib/rancher; /var/log/pods holds the
# logs of the pods it runs.
k3s.service /var/lib/rancher/
k3s.service /var/lib/kubelet/
k3s.service /var/lib/cni/
k3s.service /run/k3s/
k3s.service /var/log/pods/
k3s-agent.service /var/lib/rancher/
k3s-agent.service /var/lib/kubelet/
k3s-agent.service /var/lib/cni/
k3s-agent.service /run/k3s/
k3s-agent.service /var/log/pods/
